From: Diego Nepomuceno Marcos <me@diegonmarcos.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 15:34:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Cloud Contacts: unique applicationId
 (com.diegonmarcos.comms.contacts) via -PAPPLICATION_ID

The rebrand only changes the launcher label; without this the APK would still
install as org.fossify.contacts, colliding with a stock Fossify Contacts
install. applicationId now comes from -PAPPLICATION_ID (build.json
gradle_props), giving the fork its own package that matches
forks.contacts.app_id. namespace (R/BuildConfig package) stays
org.fossify.contacts so the code/manifest are unchanged.
---
 app/build.gradle.kts | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/app/build.gradle.kts b/app/build.gradle.kts
index 15989d57..c0c6b1a4 100644
--- a/app/build.gradle.kts
+++ b/app/build.gradle.kts
@@ -27,7 +27,13 @@ android {
     compileSdk = project.libs.versions.app.build.compileSDKVersion.get().toInt()
 
     defaultConfig {
-        applicationId = project.property("APP_ID").toString()
+        // Cloud Contacts: the INSTALLED package id. Defaults to APP_ID (stock
+        // org.fossify.contacts) but the engine passes -PAPPLICATION_ID=
+        // com.diegonmarcos.comms.contacts (build.json::forks.contacts.build.gradle_props)
+        // so our fork has its OWN unique package — it never collides with a
+        // stock Fossify Contacts install. The `namespace` (R/BuildConfig
+        // package) intentionally stays APP_ID = org.fossify.contacts (the code pkg).
+        applicationId = (project.findProperty("APPLICATION_ID") ?: project.property("APP_ID")).toString()
         minSdk = project.libs.versions.app.build.minimumSDK.get().toInt()
         targetSdk = project.libs.versions.app.build.targetSDK.get().toInt()
         versionName = project.property("VERSION_NAME").toString()
